{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Everyday Things", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "When Do You Get Up?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 4, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "Beginner", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Plural Sounds", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Let's compare sounds!", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "A vibration is a movement you can feel. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you say /s/ at the end of the word, there is no vibration. These are called unvoiced sounds because the plural and verb form \u201cs\u201d is NOT voiced (no vibration). <br /> <br />Example: <span class=\"italic\">  maps, caps, walks</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you say /z/ at the end of the word, there is a vibration. These are called voiced sounds because the plural and verb form \u201cs\u201d is voiced (vibration).<br /> <br />Example: <span class=\"italic\">plans, meals, goes</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you say the /\u026az/ sound at the end of the word, there is a vibration. These sounds make the plural and verb form \u201cs\u201d to be pronounced with an extra syllable. <br /><br />Example: <span class=\"italic\">buses, races, washes</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Vibration\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Unvoiced <span class=\\\"strong\\\">(no)</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"cats, parts, he talks\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Voiced <span class=\\\"strong\\\">(yes)</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"bells, jars, she goes\\\"